Ptyxis native split panes for Nobara / Fedora 44
================================================

Based on Fedora ptyxis-50.1-2.fc44.src.rpm, retrieved from:
https://kojipkgs.fedoraproject.org/packages/ptyxis/50.1/2.fc44/src/ptyxis-50.1-2.fc44.src.rpm
Fedora f44 dist-git commit: dce6833 (Disable inhibition management by default).
The source tarball is unmodified; the spec applies the included patches.

Package: ptyxis-50.1-2.fc44.nobara.1
This is the normal Ptyxis/Terminal package, using org.gnome.Ptyxis and the
Fedora dark-mode, accessibility, and inhibition defaults.

Shortcuts (configurable under Preferences > Shortcuts > Panes):
  Ctrl+Shift+E          Split right (side by side)
  Ctrl+Shift+O          Split down (top and bottom)
  Ctrl+Alt+Arrow        Focus neighboring pane
  Ctrl+Alt+PageDown/Up  Next/previous pane
  Ctrl+Alt+W            Close focused pane
  Ctrl+Shift+W          Close entire tab (existing shortcut)

Split and close actions are also available in the main and context menus.
Dividers can be dragged. Splits can be nested. New panes inherit the focused
pane's profile, zoom, and working directory, subject to profile settings.
Closing tabs/windows checks every pane for running commands. Exiting a shell
closes only its pane. Undo restores the most recently closed item; an undone
single pane opens as a separate tab. The existing undo timeout applies.

When session restoration is enabled, pane layouts, divider positions, focus,
profiles, titles, zoom, and directories are saved. Restoring a session starts
fresh shells, as in upstream Ptyxis; running jobs and scrollback are not
preserved. Older single-terminal saved sessions remain readable. Standalone
command windows retain single-terminal behavior.

Patches:
  0001-native-split-panes.patch    Native pane implementation and regression tests
  0002-test-with-built-agent.patch  Use the build-tree agent in GLib tests only

Build:
  dnf builddep ./ptyxis-50.1-2.fc44.nobara.1.src.rpm
  rpmbuild --rebuild ./ptyxis-50.1-2.fc44.nobara.1.src.rpm

The RPM check phase runs metadata validation, Podman parsing tests, and the
split-pane suite under Xvfb with a private D-Bus session and temporary settings.
The suite covers actual shortcut keys, nested layouts and collapsing splits,
focus, inherited directories, session/ratio restoration, legacy sessions,
inactive-pane close prompts, shell exit, undo, and tab detachment.
